+## Current activation (momentum transaction-cost robustness, campaign run 46128217530 / agent 02, task R-001)
+
+The qualified short-horizon momentum candidate (admitted 37318950814; lookback
+sweep 37361000967) was carried through a bounded transaction-cost sensitivity
+check to decide whether the edge is a gross-return artifact or survives realistic
+costs. The signal rule and universe were frozen (long the previous N-day return,
+hold 1 day, daily rebalance; lookbacks 3/5/10; 10 collected tickers); no tuning
+after seeing costs, no leverage.
+
+Predeclared cost ladder (fixed before execution): zero / realistic (the
+repository's canonical model from `examples/ma_crossover_real_data.py`:
+commission 2.0 + 0.003/share + 2c + 5bps proportional slippage) / conservative
+(2x: commission 4.0 + 0.006/share + 4c + 10bps). Each (cost level x lookback)
+cell was run through `stress_segments` (walk-forward train=252/test=84/warmup=60/
+overlap=60, 4 contiguous volatility blocks, min 400 bars/segment) with a matched
+coin-flip null at the SAME `cfg`. A-priori prediction (declared before running):
+high-turnover daily rebalancing would erode the edge for most assets.
+
+Result (artifact `state/check_artifacts/momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json`):
+- Net-of-cost candidate medians are essentially INVARIANT to the cost level. The
+  universe cross-asset median of the lookback-5 candidate medians is 0.069 at
+  zero, realistic, AND conservative.
+- Predeclared verdict-based class: COST_ROBUST=5 (AAPL, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA),
+  COST_ERODED=1 (MSFT), NO_EDGE=4 (NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM). Median-based cross-check
+  (robust to the null-dispersion label): COST_ROBUST=9, NO_EDGE=1 (NVDA).
+- Mechanism (turnover diagnostic): the persistent momentum sign rarely flips, so
+  full-sample turnover is low (~14-31x over ~17 years, <2x/yr) for most assets and
+  the conservative cost drag is only 0.02-0.09 of cumulative return. NVDA is the
+  exception (turnover 81x, drag 0.707; its negative segment deepens -0.038 ->
+  -0.088).
+- The a-priori "majority eroded" prediction is FALSIFIED: the edge is cost-robust
+  because turnover is LOW, not high.
+- The 4-asset gap between the verdict class and the median class (MSFT, JPM, JNJ,
+  XOM) is a null-dispersion label artifact, not a cost effect: their lookback-5
+  candidate medians are unchanged and positive across all cost levels; only the
+  matched null's dispersion changes, flipping the REGIME_STABLE/CONSISTENT label.
+  Recorded as a caveat.
+
+Independent verification (`verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`): Gate 1 fresh
+`walk_forward` + `noise_benchmark` recomputation (explicit per-level cfg) MATCH for
+AMZN/JPM at every cost level x lookback (candidate medians AND matched null); Gate
+2 zero-cost column cross-consistency vs `momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json`
+MATCH (all 10 tickers x 3 lookbacks); Gate 3 both cost-robustness classes
+reproduce; determinism identical. Full regression suite: 168 tests, all passing.
+
+Assessment: the short-horizon momentum edge is COST-ROBUST on the collected
+universe under the repository's realistic and 2x conservative cost model; costs do
+not erase it. The candidate positive evidence is therefore strengthened
+(cost-qualified). Bounded caveats: the "conservative" level excludes market impact
+and aggressive spread-crossing (a truly adversarial cost regime is untested), and
+the result is in-sample on one historical universe (not evidence of live
+tradeability). The next decision-relevant bound is an adversarial-cost extension
+(candidate task R-006).
